    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Lawrence Butler** anchor the lineup as our most viable producers. **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from a soft matchup against Ure\u00f1a, whose 4.65 xERA is the most exploitable on the board; his 67.71 efficiency score is bolstered by a +16% skill advantage and an ideal spot in the two-hole. **Lawrence Butler** offers the highest raw upside, with a 65.73 score driven by a +10% park factor and a +13% platoon edge against Jones. Meanwhile, **Bryson Stott** remains a high-floor play at 62.69; he is a critical component of our strategy given the slow delivery of Gusto, which creates a prime environment for **Bryson Stott** to capitalize on the league\u2019s scarcest category: stolen bases.\n\nOur most difficult decision came at the UTIL spot, where **Masyn Winn** just edged out the remaining depth on our bench. While **Masyn Winn** sits at a marginal 53.71 score, his propensity for swiping bags against a slow-working Peralta provided the necessary tie-breaker. Among those sitting on the pine, **Gavin Sheets** (53.10) was the closest to cracking the starting nine, but his unfavorable park factor and lower ceiling in the speed department kept him in the reserve pool. With the likes of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Cal Raleigh**, **Yainer Diaz**, and **Will Smith** currently languishing on the IL, our roster depth is being stretched thin, placing extra pressure on **Tyler Freeman** (58.41) to navigate a tough start against Imanaga. We will monitor the status of **Taylor Ward**, **Matt Chapman**, **Daulton Varsho**, and **Luis Arraez**, as their integration back into the daily rotation\u2014alongside prospects like **Dylan Beavers**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, and **Drew Gilbert**\u2014will be vital for closing the gap in Roto standings as we approach mid-June.",
